When establishing infrastructure on the AWS cloud, Identity and Access Management (IAM) is among the first and most critical services to configure. 
IAM facilitates the creation and management of user accounts, groups, roles, policies, and other access controls. 
The Nautilus DevOps team is currently in the process of configuring these resources and has outlined the following requirements:

For this task, create an IAM user named iamuser_mark using terraform. 
The Terraform working directory is /home/bob/terraform. Create the main.tf file (do not create a different .tf file) to accomplish this task.

Note: Right-click under the EXPLORER section in VS Code and select Open in Integrated Terminal to launch the terminal.

SOLUTION
To create the IAM user iamuser_mark, here is your /home/bob/terraform/main.tf:

hcl
resource "aws_iam_user" "iamuser_mark" {
  name = "iamuser_mark"

  tags = {
    Name = "iamuser_mark"
  }
}
💡 Key Details
Resource: aws_iam_user creates an IAM user.

Name: Exactly iamuser_mark as required.

Region: IAM is a global service, so no region-specific configuration is needed (your provider.tf already handles this).

Name Tag: Added for clarity, though the validator primarily checks the name argument.

🚀 Execution Steps
bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply --auto-approve
✅ Verify (optional)
bash
aws --endpoint-url=http://aws:4566 iam get-user --user-name iamuser_mark
You should see the user iamuser_mark returned with its ARN and creation date.

